      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=- 5 \\sin {t},\\,y'(t)=8 \\cos {2 t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(8 \\cos {2 t}\\right)}{\\left(- 5 \\sin {t}\\right)} \\\\  & =- \\frac{8 \\cos {2 t}}{5 \\sin {t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{5 \\pi}{4},$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t=\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}} & =- \\frac{8 \\cos {2 \\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}\\right)}}{5 \\sin {\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}\\right)}} \\\\  & =- \\frac{8 \\left(0\\right)}{5 \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
