      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=5 \\cos {t},\\,y'(t)=- 3 \\sin {t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(- 3 \\sin {t}\\right)}{\\left(5 \\cos {t}\\right)} \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\tan {t}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{4 \\pi}{3},$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t=\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}} & =- \\frac{3 \\tan {\\left(\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}\\right)}}{5} \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)}{5} \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
