      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=6 e^{6 t},\\,y'(t)=\\frac{1}{t + 2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{t + 2}\\right)}{\\left(6 e^{6 t}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{e^{- 6 t}}{6 \\left(t + 2\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t=1} & =\\frac{e^{- 6 \\left(1\\right)}}{6 \\left(\\left(1\\right) + 2\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18 e^{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18 e^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
