    "question": {
      ":question/id": "857f86fb-9824-5d12-98a2-c6620655bbcc",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186083243/review-0-policy-2-da51d3ee0942346e/assets/curve-1abc6cc2c24c4c776422ceeb.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\ln{\\left(3 t + 1 \\right)},\\,y=2 t e^{t},\\,- \\frac{1}{3}<t<\\infty,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=\\frac{3}{3 t + 1},\\,y'(t)=\\left(2 t + 2\\right) e^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\left(\\left(2 t + 2\\right) e^{t}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{3}{3 t + 1}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(2 t + 2\\right) \\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=0,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t=0} & =\\frac{\\left(2 \\left(0\\right) + 2\\right) \\left(3 \\left(0\\right) + 1\\right) e^{\\left(0\\right)}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
